koz VM : a local read in place must keep the value it had when the expression started finkoz

koz the right operand changes the variable, the left one keeps the old value finkoz
zafer ancien()
ouver
    keksoz a idon 1
    ran a èk (a idon 5)
fèrm
afise(ancien())

koz a call changes the variable through a closure finkoz
zafer capture()
ouver
    keksoz x idon 1
    zafer change()
    ouver
        x idon 10
        ran 100
    fèrm
    ran x èk change()
fèrm
afise(capture())

koz the left operand changes the variable, the right one sees the new value finkoz
zafer nouveau()
ouver
    keksoz b idon 1
    ran (b idon 5) èk b
fèrm
afise(nouveau())

koz a call on the right of a local that nothing captures finkoz
zafer double(n)
ouver
    ran n èk n
fèrm

zafer appel(y)
ouver
    ran y fwa double(y)
fèrm
afise(appel(3))

koz the result is stored in a variable that is also an operand finkoz
zafer carre(n)
ouver
    keksoz r idon n
    r idon r fwa r
    r idon r mwin n
    ran r
fèrm
afise(carre(4))

koz unary minus, return and condition on a local finkoz
zafer oppose(v)
ouver
    ran mwin v
fèrm
afise(oppose(3))

zafer texte(f)
ouver
    kan f
    ouver
        ran "oui"
    fèrm
    otreman
    ouver
        ran "non"
    fèrm
fèrm
afise(texte(vré))
afise(texte(fo))
